-- Post 23: Niche - Gifts for new homeowners
INSERT INTO blog_posts (title, slug, excerpt, cover_image, author, tags, published, published_at, seo_title, seo_description, seo_keywords, content)
VALUES (
  'Housewarming Gifts: What New Homeowners Actually Need',
  'housewarming-gifts-new-homeowners',
  'Know someone who just bought their first home? These practical and thoughtful gifts help them settle in without adding clutter.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1560448204-e02f11c3d0e2?w=1200&q=80',
  'The Gifted Team',
  ARRAY['Gift Ideas', 'Home', 'Milestones'],
  true,
  NOW() + INTERVAL '23 days',
  'Best Housewarming Gifts 2026 | New Homeowner Gift Ideas',
  'Find perfect housewarming gifts for new homeowners. Practical presents they actually need - from tools to luxuries for their new space.',
  ARRAY['housewarming gifts', 'new homeowner gifts', 'first home presents', 'moving in gifts', 'house gifts'],
  E'Buying a first home is exciting but expensive. New homeowners have just spent everything on deposits, fees, and probably some emergency repairs. They need practical things but might not have budget for nice versions.\n\nThe best housewarming gifts are either genuinely useful or small luxuries they wouldn''t buy themselves.\n\n## Practical Essentials\n\n### Quality Tool Kit\n\nA proper tool kit from [Stanley](https://www.stanleytools.co.uk) or [Bosch](https://www.bosch-diy.com) with essentials: hammer, screwdrivers, pliers, tape measure, level. They''ll use these forever.\n\n**Price:** £40-100\n\n### Cordless Drill\n\nA [Bosch](https://www.bosch-diy.com) or [DeWalt](https://www.dewalt.co.uk) cordless drill is essential for hanging pictures, assembling furniture, and countless DIY tasks.\n\n**Price:** £60-150\n\n![Home tools](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581783898377-1c85bf937427?w=800&q=80)\n\n### Step Ladder\n\nA quality step ladder from [Youngman](https://www.youngmangroup.com) or similar. They''ll need it for changing bulbs, painting, and reaching high shelves.\n\n**Price:** £40-80\n\n### First Aid Kit\n\nA comprehensive first aid kit for the home. [St John Ambulance](https://www.sja.org.uk) sells proper ones.\n\n**Price:** £20-40\n\n### Extension Leads\n\nQuality surge-protected extension leads from [Belkin](https://www.belkin.com) or similar. Every room needs them.\n\n**Price:** £20-40\n\n## Kitchen Upgrades\n\n### Quality Knives\n\nA good chef''s knife from [Victorinox](https://www.victorinox.com) or a small set from [ProCook](https://www.procook.co.uk). Better than the cheap ones they probably have.\n\n**Price:** £30-100\n\n### Cast Iron Pan\n\nA [Lodge](https://www.lodgecastiron.com) or [Le Creuset](https://www.lecreuset.co.uk) cast iron pan lasts forever and improves with use.\n\n**Price:** £30-200\n\n### Kitchen Scale\n\nA digital kitchen scale from [Salter](https://www.salterhousewares.co.uk) or [OXO](https://www.oxo.com). Essential for baking and cooking.\n\n**Price:** £15-30\n\n### Quality Chopping Board\n\nA large wooden board from [John Lewis](https://www.johnlewis.com) or [Joseph Joseph](https://www.josephjoseph.com). Nicer than the plastic ones they''re probably using.\n\n**Price:** £25-60\n\n## Home Comfort\n\n### Quality Bedding\n\nNice sheets from [The White Company](https://www.thewhitecompany.com), [Bedfolk](https://bedfolk.com), or [Piglet in Bed](https://pigletinbed.com). They might have skimped on bedding after spending so much on the house.\n\n**Price:** £80-200\n\n### Towel Set\n\nFluffy, quality towels from [Christy](https://www.christy.co.uk) or [The White Company](https://www.thewhitecompany.com). Good towels make a house feel like home.\n\n**Price:** £50-100\n\n### Throw Blanket\n\nA cosy throw from [The White Company](https://www.thewhitecompany.com) or [H&M Home](https://www2.hm.com) for their sofa.\n\n**Price:** £40-80\n\n![Cosy home](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1522771739844-6a9f6d5f14af?w=800&q=80)\n\n### Plants\n\nHouseplants from [Patch Plants](https://www.patchplants.com) make a new house feel lived-in. Choose low-maintenance varieties.\n\n**Price:** £20-50\n\n## Smart Home\n\n### Smart Speaker\n\nAn [Amazon Echo](https://www.amazon.co.uk) or [Google Nest](https://store.google.com) starts their smart home journey. Useful for timers, music, and controlling other devices.\n\n**Price:** £50-100\n\n### Smart Plugs\n\nA set of smart plugs from [TP-Link](https://www.tp-link.com) or [Hive](https://www.hivehome.com) lets them control lamps and devices remotely.\n\n**Price:** £20-40\n\n### Video Doorbell\n\nA [Ring](https://ring.com) or [Google Nest](https://store.google.com) doorbell for security and convenience.\n\n**Price:** £80-180\n\n## Garden & Outdoor\n\n### Quality Garden Tools\n\nBasic garden tools from [Burgon & Ball](https://www.burgonandball.com) or [Spear & Jackson](https://www.spear-and-jackson.com). Trowel, fork, secateurs—the essentials.\n\n**Price:** £40-80\n\n### Outdoor Cushions\n\nIf they have outdoor space, cushions for garden furniture from [John Lewis](https://www.johnlewis.com) or [Habitat](https://www.habitat.co.uk).\n\n**Price:** £30-60\n\n### Bird Feeder\n\nA quality bird feeder from [RSPB](https://shopping.rspb.org.uk) brings life to a new garden.\n\n**Price:** £20-40\n\n## Experiences & Services\n\n### Cleaner for a Month\n\nA few sessions with a cleaning service from [Hassle.com](https://hassle.com) while they''re still unpacking.\n\n**Price:** £60-120\n\n### Takeaway Credit\n\n[Deliveroo](https://deliveroo.co.uk) or [Uber Eats](https://www.ubereats.com) credit for when they''re too exhausted to cook.\n\n**Price:** £30-50\n\n### DIY Store Gift Card\n\n[B&Q](https://www.diy.com), [Screwfix](https://www.screwfix.com), or [Homebase](https://www.homebase.co.uk) gift cards. They''ll definitely need things.\n\n**Price:** £30-100\n\n## What to Avoid\n\n- Decorative items (they need to choose their own style)\n- Candles (unless you know their taste)\n- Anything that takes up storage space without being useful\n- Cheap versions of things (they''ll replace them)\n\n## The Thoughtful Touch\n\nInclude a card with local recommendations—best coffee shop, reliable plumber, good takeaway. Local knowledge is valuable when you''re new to an area.\n\n---\n\n*Looking for more gift inspiration? [Join the Gifted waitlist](/#signup) and discover personalised recommendations for everyone on your list.*'
)
