-- Post 27: Niche - Gifts for wine lovers
INSERT INTO blog_posts (title, slug, excerpt, cover_image, author, tags, published, published_at, seo_title, seo_description, seo_keywords, content)
VALUES (
  'Gifts for Wine Lovers: Beyond Just Another Bottle',
  'gifts-for-wine-lovers',
  'Shopping for a wine enthusiast? These gifts enhance their appreciation—from proper glassware to experiences that deepen their knowledge.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1510812431401-41d2bd2722f3?w=1200&q=80',
  'The Gifted Team',
  ARRAY['Gift Ideas', 'Wine', 'Food & Drink'],
  true,
  NOW() + INTERVAL '27 days',
  'Best Gifts for Wine Lovers 2026 | Wine Enthusiast Gift Ideas',
  'Find perfect gifts for wine lovers. From quality glassware to wine experiences, these presents go beyond just another bottle.',
  ARRAY['gifts for wine lovers', 'wine gifts', 'wine enthusiast presents', 'sommelier gifts', 'wine accessories'],
  E'Wine lovers are particular. They have preferences, opinions, and probably a cellar (or at least a wine rack) full of bottles. Buying them wine is risky—you might not match their taste or budget expectations.\n\nInstead, consider gifts that enhance their wine experience.\n\n## Glassware\n\n### Quality Wine Glasses\n\nProper glasses make a genuine difference. [Riedel](https://www.riedel.com), [Zalto](https://www.zalto.com) (the connoisseur''s choice), or [Gabriel-Glas](https://www.gabriel-glas.com) for versatile, beautiful glasses.\n\n**Price:** £30-80 per glass\n\n### Decanter\n\nA beautiful decanter from [Riedel](https://www.riedel.com), [LSA](https://www.lsa-international.com), or [Waterford](https://www.waterford.com). Both functional and decorative.\n\n**Price:** £40-150\n\n![Wine glasses](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1553361371-9b22f78e8b1d?w=800&q=80)\n\n### Champagne Glasses\n\nProper champagne flutes or coupes from [Riedel](https://www.riedel.com) or [LSA](https://www.lsa-international.com). Many wine lovers don''t have dedicated champagne glasses.\n\n**Price:** £30-60 per pair\n\n## Wine Accessories\n\n### Quality Corkscrew\n\nA proper waiter''s friend from [Laguiole](https://www.laguiole.com) or [Pulltap''s](https://www.amazon.co.uk). The tool professionals use.\n\n**Price:** £20-80\n\n### Wine Preserver\n\nThe [Coravin](https://www.coravin.com) lets them pour wine without removing the cork—preserving bottles for weeks or months. A serious gift for serious collectors.\n\n**Price:** £200-400\n\n### Wine Thermometer\n\nServing temperature matters. A wine thermometer from [Vacu Vin](https://www.vacuvin.com) or digital options help serve at the right temperature.\n\n**Price:** £10-30\n\n### Wine Aerator\n\nAn aerator from [Vinturi](https://www.vinturi.com) or [Rabbit](https://www.amazon.co.uk) for instant aeration without decanting.\n\n**Price:** £20-40\n\n## Storage & Organisation\n\n### Wine Rack\n\nA beautiful wine rack from [Made.com](https://www.made.com), [Habitat](https://www.habitat.co.uk), or [Wine Rack Store](https://www.winerackstore.co.uk).\n\n**Price:** £30-200\n\n### Wine Cellar Book\n\nA cellar book to track their collection. [Moleskine](https://www.moleskine.com) makes a wine journal, or find leather-bound options.\n\n**Price:** £15-40\n\n### Wine Fridge\n\nIf budget allows, a wine fridge from [Liebherr](https://home.liebherr.com), [Caple](https://www.caple.co.uk), or [Dunavox](https://www.dunavox.com) stores wine at proper temperature.\n\n**Price:** £200-2000\n\n## Learning & Experiences\n\n### Wine Tasting Experience\n\nA tasting at [Berry Bros & Rudd](https://www.bbr.com), [67 Pall Mall](https://www.67pallmall.com), or [Hedonism Wines](https://hedonism.co.uk).\n\n**Price:** £50-150\n\n### WSET Course\n\nA [WSET](https://www.wsetglobal.com) wine course—from beginner Level 1 to advanced. The gold standard in wine education.\n\n**Price:** £150-500\n\n![Wine tasting](https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506377247377-2a5b3b417ebb?w=800&q=80)\n\n### Vineyard Visit\n\nA tour and tasting at an English vineyard like [Nyetimber](https://www.nyetimber.com), [Ridgeview](https://www.ridgeview.co.uk), or [Gusbourne](https://www.gusbourne.com).\n\n**Price:** £30-100\n\n### Wine Subscription\n\n[The Wine Society](https://www.thewinesociety.com), [Naked Wines](https://www.nakedwines.com), or [Berry Bros](https://www.bbr.com) wine club delivers curated selections.\n\n**Price:** £50-150/month\n\n## Books\n\n### The World Atlas of Wine\n\nThe definitive wine reference by Hugh Johnson and Jancis Robinson. Essential for any serious wine lover.\n\n**Price:** £40\n\n### Wine Folly\n\n[Wine Folly](https://winefolly.com) books are accessible, visual guides to wine. Great for those still learning.\n\n**Price:** £20-30\n\n### Region-Specific Books\n\nBooks about their favourite wine region—Burgundy, Champagne, Napa Valley. Deep dives for enthusiasts.\n\n**Price:** £25-50\n\n## If You Must Buy Wine\n\n### Champagne\n\nChampagne is always appropriate. [Krug](https://www.krug.com), [Bollinger](https://www.champagne-bollinger.com), or grower Champagnes from [Lea & Sandeman](https://www.leaandsandeman.co.uk).\n\n**Price:** £40-200\n\n### Dessert Wine\n\nSauternes, Tokaji, or ice wine—something they might not buy themselves. [Berry Bros](https://www.bbr.com) can advise.\n\n**Price:** £30-100\n\n### Wine Gift Card\n\nA gift card to [Berry Bros & Rudd](https://www.bbr.com), [The Wine Society](https://www.thewinesociety.com), or [Hedonism Wines](https://hedonism.co.uk) lets them choose.\n\n**Price:** £50-200\n\n## What to Avoid\n\n- Cheap wine (they''ll know)\n- Novelty wine accessories\n- Wine from supermarkets (unless you know their taste)\n- Anything that implies they drink too much\n\n---\n\n*Looking for more gift inspiration? [Join the Gifted waitlist](/#signup) and discover personalised recommendations for everyone on your list.*'
)
